From bb65a4d606dbe31468d2179bb1583a42fd0b9450 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei <66381299+Andrei-Dr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 09:59:09 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] perf: pre-gated expert prefetch with same-step publish
 (LLAMA_MOE_PREFETCH)

During layer L of a decode step, layer L+1's router applied to layer L's MoE input predicts L+1's experts (pg1: 91% of the
actual top-8 inside a top-16 prediction; pg2: top-8 covers 70% of the misses). A CPU node at the head of layer L's host-expert
split uploads up to N predicted misses into LRU slots of layer L+1 with set_tensor_async on the compute stream (behind layer L's
cache-hit kernels, ahead of every kernel of layer L+1) and publishes them in the same step: device table copied from a pinned
stage on the same stream, host table written directly. Layer L+1 computes them on the device; the host skips them. Same math as
any cache hit. Off unless LLAMA_MOE_PREFETCH > 0; LLAMA_MOE_PREFETCH_TOPK sets the prediction width (default 16).
---
