From f43cd33d361df3a685344032db7c5e00dca06ce7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrei <66381299+Andrei-Dr@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 10:09:43 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] perf: pre-gated prefetch issues its copies on a helper
 thread, joined at the tail of the host split

pf1: prefetch raised the hit rate 48 -> 60 / 63 / 67% (budget 2 / 3 / 4) yet decode fell 3-10%: the head op issued ~3
cudaMemcpyAsync calls per expert on thread 0 under the cache lock while the other CPU threads waited at the barrier, i.e. on the
critical path. Now the head op only plans (slots, host table, table stage) and posts the copy list; a helper thread enqueues it
on the compute stream while the host experts run, and a tail node after the host down-projection waits for it, so every copy is
still in the stream before the scheduler enqueues layer L+1. Host time of both ops is logged per layer. LLAMA_MOE_PREFETCH_INLINE=1
restores the inline issue; the helper is only used on the first GPU device (it does not select a device).
---
 src/llama-graph.cpp    |   6 +++
 src/llama-moecache.cpp | 111 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 src/llama-moecache.h   |   2 +
 3 files changed, 112 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

