MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

pf1-pf3: same-step prefetch on the compute stream raises the hit rate 48 -> 67% but is 13% slower: the DMA (75 MB/token at
budget 4) lands inside the host-expert window (94%), where DDR4 is already the bottleneck, and the next device kernels wait
behind it on the stream. Window mode (default, LLAMA_MOE_PREFETCH_MODE=step keeps the old path): layer L's tail node — the host
experts just finished, the device now runs L's combine and L+1's attention, DDR4 is idle — plans layer L+2's predicted misses
(router of L+2 on L's MoE input, pg1: 83.8% recall@16) and a helper thread issues the slot and table copies on a second stream
of the device and records an event; layer L+1's tail makes the compute stream wait on it (ahead of L+1's combine, hence ahead
of L+2's cache chain). A tail node exists at every cached decode layer; a copy that reaches its target unwaited aborts. The copy
stream is drained at step(), suspend() and teardown.
